WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.907 --> 00:00:10.467
Once your school gives you a seat, the next job is to build your lesson plan library. This video shows you how, including what to do if you change your mind.

2
00:00:10.968 --> 00:00:24.568
On My Licenses, a green banner says you can pick up to forty plans. You can add more any time. If you change your mind, you can swap a plan out a limited number of times. Select Browse Lesson Plans.

3
00:00:25.069 --> 00:00:34.309
This is the full catalogue. At the top, one counter shows how many plans you've added out of your limit, and the other shows how many swaps you have left.

4
00:00:34.809 --> 00:00:40.359
To narrow the list, choose a grade level, pick a series, or type in the search box.

5
00:00:45.237 --> 00:00:48.807
When you find a lesson you want, select Add to Library.

6
00:00:49.310 --> 00:01:00.310
The first time, you're asked which grade levels you teach. Tick the ones that apply, then select Save and continue. We use them to warn you when a lesson is written for a different level.

7
00:01:00.812 --> 00:01:12.242
Next you'll see a short confirmation. If you take a plan out later, that costs one of your swaps, and the box tells you how many you have left. Select Add to My Library.

8
00:01:12.744 --> 00:01:18.604
The lesson is marked Added, and the counter goes up by one. Add a second one the same way.

9
00:01:19.106 --> 00:01:26.836
Now try a lesson written for a different level. This one is for high school, and your account is set up for elementary and middle school.

10
00:01:27.337 --> 00:01:40.157
A warning appears that says there's a curriculum level mismatch. It names the lesson's level and yours. If you want the lesson anyway, select Add anyway. If you're not sure, select Cancel, and nothing is added.

11
00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:49.060
Select My Lesson Plans to see your library. Your plans are here, and you can search them, or select View Lesson to open one.

12
00:01:49.561 --> 00:02:01.501
Changed your mind about a plan? Select Swap or remove on its card. Either choice uses one swap. In this example you have two, and the badge at the top shows how many are left.

13
00:02:02.002 --> 00:02:10.402
To replace the lesson with a different one, select Replace with another lesson. Lessons you've already assigned to your classes stay assigned.

14
00:02:10.901 --> 00:02:16.551
A banner reminds you which lesson you're replacing. Pick the new lesson and select Swap in.

15
00:02:17.051 --> 00:02:22.841
The box tells you this uses one swap and how many you'll have left. Select Swap.

16
00:02:23.342 --> 00:02:28.752
Your library now has the new lesson, and the page tells you how many swaps remain.

17
00:02:29.254 --> 00:02:36.984
To take a lesson out without replacing it, select Swap or remove again, then Remove it. That uses a swap too.

18
00:02:37.485 --> 00:02:46.575
Now the badge says no swaps left. If you try to change a lesson again, the box tells you so, and you can contact us if you need a change.

19
00:02:47.074 --> 00:02:56.884
Need more plans later? Select Add Plans. If your license is a trial, your limit can be lower than forty, and the counter at the top always shows it.
